WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.860
If you picture a warlord's Instagram,

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.500
does it look like this?

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.580
That's Ramzan Kadyrov: ruthless leader of
Chechnya

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.060
and proxy of Russian president Vladimir Putin.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.740
Here he is nuzzling a deer.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.840
These posts entertain millions of followers,

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.700
but what they mask is a dark reality.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:35.120
Kadyrov recently attracted international criticism
when reports revealed that gay Chechens

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.000
are being rounded up, tortured, and killed by authorities.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.560
At a safehouse in Moscow, a Chechen survivor
described the brutal interrogations.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.500
After the news broke, Kadyrov's spokesperson,
Alvi Karimov, denied the reports, claiming that:

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.800
Given the severity of the allegations against him,

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:21.260
it's hard to reconcile the brutality of Kadyrov's leadership

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.640
with his bizarrely entertaining online profile,

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.200
where he features animals,

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.580
celebrities,

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.280
animals and celebrities,

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.840
and, above all, his admiration for Vladimir Putin.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:45.600
What you don't see is the violence and regression
that have been rampant under his watch.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.020
Chechnya is one of 21 republics in Russia,

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.520
where regional ethnicities are allowed semi-autonomous systems of governance.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.180
It is a mountainous republic in a mostly Muslim
region of Russia known as The North Caucasus.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.210
In the 1990s, Chechnya suffered two devastating wars.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:08.700
The first was fought by separatists who tried
and failed to free Chechnya from Russian control

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.540
following the collapse of the Soviet Union.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.250
A few years later, Russia initiated a second
war to eliminate Islamist radicals who they

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.330
blamed for bombings that killed hundreds 
 of Russian civilians.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:25.799
The war was brutal and Putin's forces
destroyed Grozny, the capital of Chechnya.

00:02:25.799 --> 00:02:31.600
Putin later placed Akhmad Kadyrov, Ramzan's
father, in charge of rebuilding the republic.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:37.420
Akhmad became President of Chechnya in October 2003, but the insurgency continued

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:45.040
and in 2004 Kadyrov was killed when Islamist separatists bombed a parade he was watching in Grozny

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:50.720
After the bombing, Ramzan was swiftly ushered to Moscow, where he met Putin that same day.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.440
At the time, he was leading Chechen security
forces and had been blamed for several kidnappings.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.840
But, despite the allegations, Putin positioned
him for leadership

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.260
and he has been ruling the republic ever since 2007.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.240
In that time, Putin has given Kadyrov ample funding in exchange for

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.440
keeping the Chechen conflict under control.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.620
The Kremlin funds at least 80% of Chechnya's annual budget

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.280
and Ramzan Kadyrov spends that money lavishly

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:25.739
Not only on himself, but also on construction
projects he constantly promotes.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:29.740
He often features Akhmad Kadyrov Mosque,

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:33.960
an opulent building named after his father that symbolizes both Chechen renewal

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.880
and Ramzan's self-proclaimed commitment to Islam.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.640
He has also used the money to fund an army
of loyalists called the "Kadyrovtsy:

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.150
a militia that has roots in the security forces
he ran for his father.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:54.340
On Instagram he touts their strength and discipline,
offering a clear threat to possible insurgents.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.140
So far, his methods have delivered results.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:01.730
Kadyrov has brought down Islamist violence
in Chechnya, which has solidified his authority

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:06.340
and served as a major political victory for Putin.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:10.700
Part of his strategy has been promoting a
strict interpretation of Islam.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.980
Online, he maintains a steady stream of overtly religious posts and in public statements

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.640
he insists that women wear headscarves and has supported honor killings

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.530
as part of what he calls a "virtue
campaign".

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.000
He has also endorsed men shooting women on
the street with paintball guns

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.160
when they are not fully covered, like in this YouTube video.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:36.910
In addition to shaping his Islamic agenda,
Kadyrov uses social media to craft a warrior

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:42.160
persona that is based in historical notions
of Chechen identity.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.980
It's an identity that can be traced back
to the early 20th century,

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:51.140
when Leo Tolstoy wrote about the Chechen rebellion in his book "Hadji Murad".

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:56.160
Ever since then, ethnic Russians have perceived
Chechens as fierce warriors.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.920
And that image has played out over the course of history:

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.040
From the two Chechen wars...

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.740
...to the more recent photos of Chechens
fighting for ISIS in the Middle East.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:13.520
Now, copies of Tolstoy's novel come with
a photo of a modern soldier on the cover.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.900
The tough guy stereotype has also travelled
beyond Russia.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:20.660
It is telling that a mobster in "The Dark Knight"
is known simply as "The Chechen".

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:32.940
Scrolling through his feed, you can see that
Kadyrov channels that identity

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:36.900
with training montages,

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.220
martial arts clips,

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.400
fitness selfies,

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.700
"Sport!"

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:46.080
and close encounters with threatening creatures.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.900
But Kadyrov also poses as the benevolent leader
of Chechnya,

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:56.900
who enjoys quiet moments with animals,

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:01.260
bike rides,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:06.420
playing with his friends,

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:11.710
And performing the "Lezginka",
a regional dance.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.860
He also poses as Chechnya's biggest advocate,

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:20.140
and has paid for several Western celebrities to visit Grozny.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.860
Past visitors have included the boxer Floyd
Mayweather,

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.320
the actor Steven Seagal,

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.200
and the actress Hilary Swank,

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.660
"...a great honor to learn more about you and your country and what you're building."

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.380
who visited for Kadyrov's birthday in 2011.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.480
"Happy Birthday Mr. President!"

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.380
Apart from hosting celebrities,

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:50.620
Kadyrov constantly leverages his relationship with Putin to bolster his authority.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:55.360
On Instagram, he regularly demonstrates his
allegiance to the Russian President.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:58.620
But at times, his enthusiasm backfires.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.340
He once framed a photo of a Putin critic between
the crosshairs of a rifle scope,

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:09.180
a reckless provocation that led some people to wonder
if Putin might be losing control of Kadyrov.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.140
These missteps do not go unnoticed.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:15.120
Kadyrov's nearly three million followers on Instagram

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.620
are around twice the entire population of Chechnya.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:21.740
Some of his posts have already led to repercussions
from Moscow.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:26.800
In October, he proudly posted this clip from
an MMA fight featuring ten year-old boys,

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.840
including his own sons.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:35.160
In response, Russia's ministry of sport
launched an investigation into the event

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:39.500
and later that month, Anton Siluanov, Putin's
finance minister,

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.980
announced possible cuts to the Chechen budget.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:48.260
Now, revelations about Kadyrov's persecution
of gays have caused global protests

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.220
and created fresh tensions.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.820
At a recent meeting, German Chancellor Angela Merkel

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:58.080
called on Putin to discipline his Chechen subordinate.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:22.400
By then, Putin had already summoned Kadyrov
to the Kremlin for a meeting,

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:27.500
but whether this did anything to change Kadyrov's behavior remains to be seen.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:33.120
For the time being, Kadyrov continues to be
Putin's man in Chechnya

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:38.180
and as long as he can keep the region stable, things are likely to stay that way.

